{
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "autoloader-generic",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [],
      "lines": [
        "The app ships no composer/autoload.php, so the server registers its generic loader for lib/ and looks every class up in the file system.",
        "  A composer/composer.json with config.vendor-dir \".\", config.optimize-autoloader true, a config.autoloader-suffix and autoload.psr-4 {\"OCA\\\\People\\\\\": \"../lib/\"} makes composer dump-autoload write composer/autoload.php with a class map; the code of the app does not change."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "route-target-missing",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [
        "GET /index.php/apps/people/search/{search}  people.contact.search  appinfo/routes.php:10 routes: OCA\\People\\Controller\\ContactController has no method search()",
        "GET /index.php/apps/people/list/{id}  people.contact.list  appinfo/routes.php:10 routes: OCA\\People\\Controller\\ContactController has no method list()"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "2 routes name a controller class or a method that does not exist, or a method that is not public. A request to such a route ends in an error.",
        "  GET /index.php/apps/people/search/{search}  people.contact.search  appinfo/routes.php:10 routes: OCA\\People\\Controller\\ContactController has no method search()",
        "  GET /index.php/apps/people/list/{id}  people.contact.list  appinfo/routes.php:10 routes: OCA\\People\\Controller\\ContactController has no method list()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "dev-tools-in-root",
      "level": "info",
      "places": [],
      "lines": [
        "phpunit/phpunit is in require-dev of composer.json. The manual recommends a vendor-bin/ of bamarni/composer-bin-plugin per tool, so that the dependencies of a tool cannot conflict with those of the app."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "template-inline-style",
      "level": "info",
      "places": [
        "templates/content/index.php:104 style= attribute",
        "templates/content/index.php:141 style= attribute"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "2 inline styles in templates/. The default Content Security Policy of the server allows inline style; a response whose policy disallows it drops them. A stylesheet added with OCP\\Util::addStyle() holds in both cases.",
        "  templates/content/index.php:104 style= attribute",
        "  templates/content/index.php:141 style= attribute"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "time-direct",
      "level": "info",
      "places": [
        "lib/Controller/ContactController.php:103 new DateTime()",
        "lib/Controller/ContactController.php:151 new DateTime()",
        "lib/Controller/SettingController.php:112 new DateTime()"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "lib/ reads the clock directly in 3 places. OCP\\AppFramework\\Utility\\ITimeFactory, a PSR-20 ClockInterface, gives the same time and can be replaced in a test.",
        "  lib/Controller/ContactController.php:103 new DateTime()",
        "  lib/Controller/ContactController.php:151 new DateTime()",
        "  lib/Controller/SettingController.php:112 new DateTime()"
      ]
    },
